e":60},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]},{"groundTruth":{"original_line":1162,"line":1162,"comment_lines":["[][1162]"],"review_comment":["Could be `v.before(INTRODUCING_UNSIGNED_LONG)` instead","Ah, `SqlVersion` doesn\u0027t implement `VersionId`. If it implements `VersionId\u003cT\u003e` then this method will come for free","Right, there\u0027s no `.before()` method and `SqlVersion` can\u0027t implement `VersionId\u003cT\u003e`, since it\u0027s in a package very light in dependencies."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/sql/qa/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/sql/qa/rest/RestSqlTestCase.java","id":35353,"created_at":"2024-10-10T08:51:51Z","original_position":44,"side":"RIGHT","position":44,"submitted_on_commit":"452e3b04e2e07888bdc7ae779f2f319d49e7b8d1","diff_hunk":"@@ -1159,7 +1159,8 @@ public void testBinaryFieldFiltering() throws IOException {\n \n     public void testPreventedUnsignedLongMaskedAccess() throws IOException {\n         loadUnsignedLongTestData();\n-        Version version \u003d VersionUtils.randomVersionBetween(random(), null, VersionUtils.getPreviousVersion(INTRODUCING_UNSIGNED_LONG));\n+        var preVersionCompat \u003d SqlVersions.getAllVersions().stream().filter(v -\u003e v.onOrAfter(INTRODUCING_UNSIGNED_LONG) \u003d\u003d false).toList();","submitted_line":1162},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]},{"groundTruth":{"original_line":205,"line":205,"comment_lines":["[][205]"],"review_comment":["This is the `minCompatibleShardNode` - which is still a `Version`. If the version is locked at 8.16, this means this parameter can be completely removed on v9 and replaced with another mechanism if/when SQL needs to be updated?","\u003e this means this parameter can be completely removed on v9\r\n\r\nI would think so, assuming that we have an upgrade procedure to 9.x similar to [the existing 7.x to 8.x one](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elastic-stack/current/upgrading-elastic-stack.html#prepare-to-upgrade): upgrade to the latest 8.x one and then the target 9.x. Th